# UI/UX Design System Rules

Design direction:
- User-centered
- Vietnamese-first
- Mobile-first
- Modern fintech-inspired
- Friendly
- Soft
- Rounded
- Clean
- Easy to scan

Core UI style:
- Use rounded corners consistently.
- Prefer large border radius.
- Use soft cards.
- Use clean spacing.
- Use clear visual hierarchy.
- Avoid clutter.
- Avoid sharp, harsh, enterprise-looking UI.

Rounded design:
- Cards should have rounded corners.
- Buttons should have rounded corners.
- Text fields should have rounded corners.
- Dialogs should have rounded corners.
- Bottom sheets should have rounded top corners.
- Chips and filters should be pill-shaped where appropriate.

Recommended border radius:
- Small components: 12
- Inputs and buttons: 16
- Cards: 20
- Bottom sheets and dialogs: 24
- Large containers: 24-32

Spacing:
- Use generous whitespace.
- Avoid cramped layouts.
- Keep related items visually grouped.
- Use consistent spacing scale.

Suggested spacing scale:
- 4
- 8
- 12
- 16
- 20
- 24
- 32

User-centered UX:
- Important actions should require minimal taps.
- Adding an expense should be fast.
- The amount input should be prominent.
- Category selection should be easy.
- Date selection should default to today.
- Recent categories should be easy to access.
- Avoid forcing users through unnecessary steps.

Expense input UX:
- Amount field should be the main focus.
- Default transaction type can be expense.
- Date should default to today.
- Category should be visually selectable.
- Save button should be obvious.
- Validation should appear close to the problematic field.

Dashboard UX:
- Show key information first:
  - Total expense this month
  - Total income this month
  - Balance
  - Top spending categories
  - Recent transactions
- Avoid showing too many charts at once.
- Financial data should be easy to scan quickly.

Charts:
- Charts must be simple.
- Avoid overly complex visualizations.
- Labels must be readable in Vietnamese.
- Use charts only when they help understanding.
- Do not make charts visually overwhelming.

Accessibility:
- Text must be readable.
- Tap targets must be large enough.
- Contrast must work in light and dark mode.
- Do not rely only on color to communicate meaning.
- Important icons should have labels or tooltips where appropriate.

Animations:
- Use smooth and lightweight animations.
- Do not overuse animations.
- Animations should support usability, not distract.
